WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.060
Deep nuclei that never reach the spinal cord still decide, in the classic model,

2
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.700
whether a movement goes ahead.

3
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:14.080
How? Their output neurons, in GPi, fire steadily.

4
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.980
They hold the thalamus under constant inhibition, like a foot resting on a brake.

5
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.120
Movement needs the brake lifted.

6
00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:23.773
Two routes reach that brake.

7
00:00:24.353 --> 00:00:28.933
In the direct pathway, striatal neurons with D1 receptors inhibit GPi.

8
00:00:28.933 --> 00:00:33.273
Give each excitatory link +1, and each inhibitory link −1.

9
00:00:33.893 --> 00:00:36.253
Then multiply along the route.

10
00:00:36.253 --> 00:00:40.553
+1, times −1, times −1, times +1.

11
00:00:41.013 --> 00:00:42.313
The product is +1.

12
00:00:42.313 --> 00:00:45.153
Two inhibitions in series give disinhibition.

13
00:00:46.283 --> 00:00:48.383
The indirect pathway has more steps.

14
00:00:49.243 --> 00:00:52.183
Striatal neurons with D2 receptors inhibit GPe.

15
00:00:52.183 --> 00:00:56.143
GPe inhibits the subthalamic nucleus, STN.

16
00:00:56.283 --> 00:00:58.143
The STN excites GPi.

17
00:00:58.143 --> 00:01:04.103
Multiply again. Plus one, minus one, minus one, plus one, minus one, plus one.

18
00:01:04.583 --> 00:01:05.943
The product is −1.

19
00:01:05.943 --> 00:01:08.963
This route ends up decreasing cortical drive.

20
00:01:09.967 --> 00:01:13.807
Now add dopamine from the substantia nigra, pars compacta.

21
00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:17.607
In the classic model, it excites the D1 direct neurons.

22
00:01:18.227 --> 00:01:20.507
It inhibits the D2 indirect neurons.

23
00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:23.867
Exciting a +1 route raises cortical drive.

24
00:01:24.327 --> 00:01:26.807
Inhibiting a −1 route also raises it.

25
00:01:27.347 --> 00:01:29.047
Both actions push toward movement.

26
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:33.490
So losing dopamine pushes both routes toward less movement.

27
00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.290
The direct route weakens.

28
00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:37.210
The indirect route strengthens.

29
00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:43.090
GPe is more inhibited, the STN is released, and GPi fires more.

30
00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.370
The thalamus is held down harder.

31
00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:49.170
The model predicts akinesia, as in Parkinson's disease.

32
00:01:50.283 --> 00:01:53.003
This is a way to reason about the direction of a change.

33
00:01:53.523 --> 00:01:56.243
It is not a measured law of how firing rates add.

34
00:01:56.243 --> 00:01:57.563
And the model strains.

35
00:01:58.403 --> 00:02:02.783
In mice, calcium signals from both pathways rose around the start of an action.

36
00:02:03.363 --> 00:02:05.463
It also gives no account of rest tremor.

37
00:02:06.123 --> 00:02:10.943
Keep the rule: multiply the signs to predict direction, and remember it is a model.
